      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;spiritual-paths-richard-sylvester&#34;&gt;Spiritual Paths Richard Sylvester&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Source: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/discourses/teachers/paths_sylvester.htm&#34;&gt;TW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Author: Richard Sylvester&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0955176212/fromtheunreat-20&#34;&gt;&lt;figure class=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/images/hope_you_die.jpg&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;img src=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/images/hope_you_die.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;book cover&#34; title=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &#xA;&#xA;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Visit &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.richardsylvester.com&#34;&gt;Richard Sylvester&amp;rsquo;s &amp;rsquo;s website&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Link to entry on &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/teachers/neo_teachers1.htm#sylvester&#34;&gt;Teacher&amp;rsquo;s page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Link to listing on &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/reading/read_neo.htm#sylvester&#34;&gt;Recommended Books page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The following is extracted from the above book, &amp;lsquo;I Hope You Die Soon: words on non-duality&amp;rsquo;, which can be purchased from Amazon.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;However you wake up, whether it&amp;rsquo;s with a shock or gently, there&amp;rsquo;s still that certainty that what was known to be real while you were asleep is actually unreal. We could use lucid dreaming as a metaphor for liberation, because in lucid dreaming the night-time dreamer knows that it&amp;rsquo;s a dream.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
